course: dictionary
lesson: 11168
title: Proper nouns: Windsor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Windsor is a proper noun. It is the name of one particular thing, here a town, a castle or a family, so it starts with a capital letter. Look for clues around it to find out which one the writer means.
explain: «The Thames rises in the Cotswold hills and flows through Oxford, Reading and Windsor.» Oxford and Reading are towns, so Windsor is a town too, one that sits beside the river.
explain: «Prince Harry married Meghan Markle at St George's Chapel, Windsor.» This sentence has a royal wedding in it, so Windsor is the place where the chapel is. When Windsor appears in a story about kings, queens or royal families, it may mean the royal family itself. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence.
fact: Windsor is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: «Windsor» means a town in Berkshire, England, west of London, by the River Thames, and it is the home of «Windsor Castle».
fact: «Windsor Castle» is a very old castle and one of the official homes of the British king or queen.
fact: «The Windsors» or «the House of Windsor» is the family name of the British royal family.
fact: «Windsor» also means a city in Ontario, Canada, opposite Detroit.
exercise: «The Thames... flows through Oxford, Reading and Windsor.» What kind of word is Windsor here? | *A town by the river | A colour | A type of bird
exercise: «Prince Harry married Meghan Markle at St George's Chapel, Windsor.» What does this sentence tell you about Windsor? | It means a happy feeling | *It names a place where a royal wedding happened | It is a kind of boat
exercise: Nan says «the Windsors» while watching the news. Who does she mean? | A family on holiday in Canada | A group of football fans | *The British royal family
test: The word Windsor starts with a capital letter because it is a what? | adjective | *proper noun | common noun | verb
test: «Windsor Castle» is one of the official homes of whom? | The Canadian prime minister | A famous explorer | *The British king or queen
exam: In Canada, Windsor is a city in Ontario, opposite which American city? | Chicago | New York | Los Angeles | *Detroit
